-- title:
--   Quotients of W[[X₁,…,Xₙ]] are Noetherian and adically complete
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring which is local, Noetherian, and complete for the $\mathfrak m_W$-adic topology in the strong sense of `IsAdicComplete` (i.e. Hausdorff and complete with respect to the filtration by the powers of the maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_W =$ `maximalIdeal W`). Let $n$ be a natural number and let $J$ be an arbitrary ideal of the ring $R :=$ `MvPowerSeries (Fin n) W` of formal power series over $W$ in $n$ commuting variables indexed by `Fin n`. The conclusion is the conjunction of two assertions about the quotient ring $S := R/J$: first, $S$ is a Noetherian ring; second, $S$ is adically complete with respect to the ideal $\mathfrak M S$, where $\mathfrak M$ is the maximal ideal of the local ring $R$ (that is, the ideal generated by $\mathfrak m_W$ together with the variables) and $\mathfrak M S$ denotes its image under the quotient map $R \to S$. No hypothesis is imposed on $J$; in particular $J$ may be the unit ideal, and $n$ may be $0$.
--
--   This is the standard statement that quotients of a formal power series ring over a complete Noetherian local ring are again complete Noetherian local rings (for the image of the maximal ideal), combining the Noetherianity and completeness of $W[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]$ with the fact that adic completeness passes to quotients of complete Noetherian rings. It is used in the analysis of Drinfeld charts, where the coordinate ring of a chart is presented as such a quotient and its $\mathfrak m$-adic completeness is required.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_isNoetherianRing_and_isAdicComplete_map_maximalIdeal_quotient.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
